    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408">

                <pb facs="0898" n="814" xml:id="pg814"/>

                <head>No. 403.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Curry.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-10-20"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 20,
                        1886</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 128.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 119 of the 29th ultimo is
                    received. The memorandum on the subject of the differential flag duty sent by
                    you to the foreign office, a copy of which you inclose, is a clear and distinct
                    statement of the issue.</p>
                <p>With regard to the possibility of a renewed <hi rendition="#italic">modus
                        vivendi</hi>, instructions are deferred, as the cable, being now necessarily
                    called into requisition, anticipates any communications by mail.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
